{"id":"000VKZ","title":"Boulder Roll : Locusts","author":"Artham","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-18T18:40:21+00:00","posted":"Heute, 18:37 Uhr","rules":"Boulder rolls are back after Boulder roll: heat, and now, they're Renban !\n\nBoulder roll : Locusts - Sudokupad\n\nFill the grid with digits from 1 to 9 so that no digit repeats in a region. Digits might repeat in a row or column.\n\nBoulder Roll: Each boulder will enter the grid and roll in a straight line along its row or column until it exits the opposite side of the grid. As it rolls, it imprints a repeating sequence of digits onto the cells it passes through. The boulder's size determines how many cells it must traverse to complete one roll. For example, a size-4 boulder entering from the left edge of a row might imprint the digits 1-3-4-2-1-3-4-2-1 in its row.\n\nRenban Boulders: In this puzzle, boulders behave like renban lines. A boulder's one-roll sequence must contain a set of consecutive digits without repeats, in any order.\n\nConsecutive Kropki: If two digits are separated by a scarab, they are consecutive.\n\nRatio Kropki: If two digits are separated by a scorpion, one is double the other.\n\nClones: If two digits are separated by a locust, they are identical.\n\nExtra region: Digits on cactuses are all different.","solutionCode":"Row 6 from left to right","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/vbi9oq0k2x","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/vbi9oq0k2x","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-18T18:40:21+00:00"}